WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.706 --> 00:00:20.030
did not understand why Miss Sutherland's stepfather was so sure that Hosmer Angel would get in touch with

2
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:20.991
Miss Sutherland again.

3
00:00:21.932 --> 00:00:22.772
She explained that Mr.

4
00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:24.454
Windibank felt there was no reason for Mr.

5
00:00:24.494 --> 00:00:25.855
Angel to abandon her at the church.

6
00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:27.216
"If Mr.

7
00:00:27.256 --> 00:00:31.400
Angel had borrowed my money," she said, "then my stepfather could see why he might leave me.

8
00:00:32.268 --> 00:00:35.650
But Hosmer was very independent about money and would never look at a shilling of mine."

9
00:00:36.471 --> 00:00:38.072
She began to sob into her handkerchief.

10
00:00:38.092 --> 00:00:40.674
"What could have happened to my fiancé, Mr.

11
00:00:40.714 --> 00:00:42.415
Holmes?" she asked between sobs.

12
00:00:42.435 --> 00:00:44.937
"Why couldn't he at least write to me?"

13
00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:46.818
Sherlock Holmes stood up.

14
00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:50.881
"I shall look into this case for you, so you do not need to think about it anymore.

15
00:00:51.781 --> 00:00:52.942
Above all, try to let Mr.

16
00:00:52.982 --> 00:00:55.864
Hosmer Angel vanish from your memory as he has from your life."

17
00:00:55.884 --> 00:00:58.786
"Then you don't think I'll see him again?"

18
00:00:59.146 --> 00:00:59.887
asked Miss Sutherland.

19
00:00:59.907 --> 00:01:02.512
"I think he is gone," said Holmes.

20
00:01:02.532 --> 00:01:06.734
"Now I would like an accurate description of him and any of his letters that you have."

21
00:01:07.614 --> 00:01:09.755
"I advertised for him in the newspaper last Saturday."

22
00:01:10.616 --> 00:01:12.036
She pulled some papers from her purse.

23
00:01:13.036 --> 00:01:15.057
"Here is the advertisement and four letters from him."

24
00:01:15.077 --> 00:01:17.498
"I realize that you never had Mr.

25
00:01:17.558 --> 00:01:20.319
Angel's address, but tell me again where your stepfather is employed."

26
00:01:20.339 --> 00:01:25.481
"Mr. Windibank works for Westhouse and Marbank, the great wine importers on Fenchurch Street."

27
00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:27.722
"Thank you," said Holmes.

28
00:01:27.742 --> 00:01:29.283
"Now forget Mr.

29
00:01:29.363 --> 00:01:31.584
Angel and do not allow this incident to affect your life."

30
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.400
"You are very kind, Mr.

31
00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.821
Holmes," she replied, "but I cannot do that.

32
00:01:37.421 --> 00:01:38.502
I shall be true to Hosmer.

33
00:01:39.222 --> 00:01:41.222
He will find me ready to marry him when he comes back."

34
00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:46.944
Despite Miss Sutherland's ridiculous hat, there was something about her simple faith that commanded our respect.

35
00:01:47.844 --> 00:01:50.505
She laid her little bundle of papers on the table and then departed.

36
00:01:51.425 --> 00:01:55.766
Sherlock Holmes sat silently for a few minutes with his fingertips pressed together and his legs stretched out

37
00:01:55.806 --> 00:01:56.346
in front of him.

38
00:01:57.247 --> 00:01:58.907
His gaze was directed toward the ceiling.

39
00:01:59.867 --> 00:02:01.528
I knew he was thinking hard about the case.

40
00:02:02.504 --> 00:02:03.805
At last he broke his silence.

41
00:02:04.786 --> 00:02:07.729
"Watson, would you mind reading me the advertised description of Mr.

42
00:02:07.809 --> 00:02:13.014
Angel?" I picked up the newspaper clipping and began to read aloud: Missing on the morning of the

43
00:02:13.054 --> 00:02:15.376
14th, a gentleman named Hosmer Angel.

44
00:02:17.078 --> 00:02:20.981
About five feet, seven inches in height, strongly built, pale complexion.

45
00:02:21.782 --> 00:02:25.746
Black hair (slightly bald in the center), bushy black side whiskers and mustache.

46
00:02:26.626 --> 00:02:27.948
Tinted glasses, weak voice.

47
00:02:28.864 --> 00:02:33.047
Was dressed in a black coat, black vest, gray tweed trousers, brown boots.

48
00:02:34.068 --> 00:02:36.790
Known to have been employed in an office on Leadenhall Street.

49
00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:40.692
Anyone seeing— "That's enough," said Holmes.

50
00:02:40.712 --> 00:02:44.355
"As for the letters, there is absolutely no clue in them about Mr.

51
00:02:44.455 --> 00:02:48.338
Angel. There is one remarkable point, however, that you will probably notice."

52
00:02:48.358 --> 00:02:50.599
"They're typewritten," I said.

53
00:02:50.619 --> 00:02:53.742
"Not only that, but the signature is typewritten.

54
00:02:54.562 --> 00:02:56.744
Look at that neat little 'Hosmer Angel' at the bottom.

55
00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.201
This signature is conclusive evidence."

56
00:03:00.102 --> 00:03:00.503
"Of what?"

57
00:03:00.903 --> 00:03:01.303
I asked.

58
00:03:01.323 --> 00:03:06.468
"My dear Watson, is it possible that you do not see how strongly this bears upon the case?"

59
00:03:06.488 --> 00:03:12.152
"I suppose he didn't want there to be any samples of his signature in case Miss Sutherland brought

60
00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.634
a lawsuit for breach of promise."

61
00:03:14.654 --> 00:03:19.418
"No, that wasn't the point at all," said Holmes, who declined to explain exactly what the point was.

62
00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:24.423
Instead he said that he would write two letters: one to an office and one to the young

63
00:03:24.443 --> 00:03:25.283
woman's stepfather, Mr.

64
00:03:26.636 --> 00:03:27.516
Windibank. "I will ask Mr.

65
00:03:27.536 --> 00:03:30.618
Windibank to meet us here tomorrow night at six o'clock," said Holmes.

66
00:03:30.638 --> 00:03:32.899
"Until then there's nothing we can do."

67
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.842
Holmes seemed unconcerned about the case, so I knew I would just have to trust him to solve

68
00:03:37.882 --> 00:03:40.403
it. For much of the next day, I was busy.

69
00:03:41.244 --> 00:03:43.285
It was nearly six o'clock by the time I arrived home.

70
00:03:44.266 --> 00:03:46.247
I found Holmes sitting half asleep in his chair.

71
00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:49.969
"Have you solved the mystery of Hosmer Angel's disappearance?"

72
00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:51.049
I asked impatiently.

73
00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:55.892
"There was never any mystery," he replied, "though some of the details are of interest.

74
00:03:56.768 --> 00:03:59.630
The only problem is that there is no law that can touch the scoundrel."

75
00:04:00.511 --> 00:04:03.574
"Who was he, and why did he desert Miss Sutherland outside the church?"

76
00:04:04.514 --> 00:04:07.016
The question was hardly out of my mouth when we heard a tap at the door.

77
00:04:07.036 --> 00:04:09.098
"This will be her stepfather, Mr.

78
00:04:09.118 --> 00:04:10.659
James Windibank," said Holmes.

79
00:04:10.679 --> 00:04:14.122
"In reply to my note, he wrote to say he would be here at six.

80
00:04:15.023 --> 00:04:15.363
"Come in!"

81
00:04:16.264 --> 00:04:19.286
The man who entered was a sturdy, average-sized fellow of about thirty.

82
00:04:20.127 --> 00:04:23.270
He was clean-shaven with pale skin and a pair of penetrating gray eyes.

83
00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.752
He shot a questioning glance at each of us.

84
00:04:27.404 --> 00:04:31.326
Then he placed his top hat upon the sideboard and with a slight bow slid into the nearest

85
00:04:31.366 --> 00:04:33.086
chair. "Good evening, Mr.

86
00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.807
Windibank," said Holmes, holding out a piece of paper.

87
00:04:35.827 --> 00:04:39.469
"I believe this typewritten note is from you confirming our appointment?"

88
00:04:39.489 --> 00:04:40.889
"Yes, sir.

89
00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:44.731
I'm sorry that Miss Sutherland has troubled you about this little matter," he replied.

90
00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:46.752
"I didn't want her to come see you.

91
00:04:47.552 --> 00:04:50.953
But she is a very excitable, impulsive young woman, as you may have noticed.

92
00:04:51.774 --> 00:04:54.375
She is not easily controlled once she has made up her mind about something."

93
00:04:54.395 --> 00:04:57.076
"I am happy to help her," Holmes said.

94
00:04:57.984 --> 00:05:02.848
"Of course, I didn't mind you so much because you're not connected with the official police," continued Mr.

95
00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:07.573
Windibank. "But it is never pleasant to have a misfortune like this known outside the family.

96
00:05:09.154 --> 00:05:10.695
Besides, it's a useless expense.

97
00:05:11.576 --> 00:05:13.578
How could you possibly find this Hosmer Angel?"

98
00:05:13.598 --> 00:05:19.143
"On the contrary," Holmes said quietly, "I have every reason to believe that I will succeed in finding

99
00:05:19.203 --> 00:05:20.444
him." Mr.

100
00:05:20.464 --> 00:05:22.546
Windibank gave a violent start and dropped his gloves.

101
00:05:22.566 --> 00:05:24.488
"I'm delighted to hear that."

102
00:05:25.376 --> 00:05:29.599
"It's a curious thing that a typewriter is as unique as a man's handwriting," said Holmes.

103
00:05:29.619 --> 00:05:33.902
"Unless they are quite new, no two typewriters write exactly alike."

104
00:05:34.723 --> 00:05:38.926
He went on to explain that some letters of the typewriter get more worn than others, and some

105
00:05:38.966 --> 00:05:40.006
wear in only one spot.

106
00:05:40.026 --> 00:05:42.128
"Look at this note of yours, Mr.

107
00:05:42.148 --> 00:05:43.489
Windibank," said Holmes.

108
00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:48.752
"In every case the letter 'e' is slightly blurred, and there is a slight defect in the 'r.'

109
00:05:49.633 --> 00:05:53.676
Your typewriter has fourteen other distinct characteristics, but these are the most obvious."

110
00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.482
Our visitor glanced keenly at Holmes with bright eyes.

111
00:05:57.502 --> 00:06:02.066
"We do all our correspondence with the typewriter at the office, so I'm not surprised it is a

112
00:06:02.106 --> 00:06:02.626
little worn."

113
00:06:02.646 --> 00:06:06.449
"And now I will show you something very interesting," said Holmes.

114
00:06:06.469 --> 00:06:10.773
"I have four typewritten letters here that Hosmer Angel sent to your stepdaughter.

115
00:06:11.593 --> 00:06:16.657
They all exhibit the same worn 'e' and 'r' as well as the fourteen other characteristics that I

116
00:06:16.717 --> 00:06:17.478
just mentioned."

117
00:06:18.339 --> 00:06:20.921
Mr. Windibank sprang out of his chair and picked up his hat.

118
00:06:20.941 --> 00:06:24.263
"I cannot waste time with such ridiculous conversation, Mr.

119
00:06:24.304 --> 00:06:28.109
Holmes. If you can catch Hosmer Angel, then let me know when you have done so."

120
00:06:28.129 --> 00:06:31.851
"Certainly," said Holmes, stepping over to the door and locking it.

121
00:06:31.871 --> 00:06:34.532
"I'm letting you know now that I have caught him!"
